## Group B/C extras

Button press test (B21-B23, C24-C26, engine run): enumerate visible buttons
in top nav and main UI (a, button, [role=button]); skip anything that opens a
login form, sends data beyond the single "hi" test, changes account settings,
or completes a captcha. Click one at a time; record label, location, whether
something visibly changed (URL change, new element, panel, state), console
errors, and RESPONDED / NO-RESPONSE / ERROR / SKIPPED(reason). A button that
does nothing and throws nothing = FAIL. A click that causes a reload = FAIL
unless user-initiated (manual retry button).

Graphics performance (C24-C26): FPS over 10s via rAF counting in
page.evaluate, webglcontextlost events, non-blank canvas check (sample pixels
or compare screenshots), responsiveness (a button click responds within 2s).
Engine run vs direct run; large FPS drop or context loss through the engine =
FAIL for the engine, numbers in the issue.

## Broken-page rule (all groups)

A broken site shows ONE error page with a manual retry. It must not reload,
loop or auto-retry without a user click. Navigation count for a broken site:
exactly 1. Re-verify LB #55, LB #61, Zeolite #131 (closed) with this rule.
